          "cachedResultName": "Gemini 3.5 Flash Lite"
        },
        "text": "Review this contract from the perspective of the distributor (second party).\n\nIdentify the main legal and commercial risks for the distributor.\n\nFor each risk, provide ONLY the following:\n1. Contract Clause: identify the relevant clause number and quote the relevant part briefly.\n2. Risk: explain clearly why this clause is risky for the distributor.\n3. Proposed Clause: draft a revised clause that provides better protection to the distributor.\n\nFocus on:\n- Unlimited or excessive liability\n- Payment obligations\n- Penalties and indemnities\n- Termination rights\n- Exclusivity\n- Minimum purchase obligations\n- Product returns\n- Delivery and supply obligations\n- Compliance and sanctions\n- Intellectual property\n- Confidentiality\n- Governing law and dispute resolution\n- Force majeure\n- Any obligation that is one-sided against the distributor\n\nDo not give a general summary of the contract.\nDo not invent clause numbers or obligations that are not present in the contract.\nIf a risk is not clearly supported by the contract, do not include it.\n\nCRITICAL OUTPUT FORMAT:\nOutput ONLY a complete, valid, self-contained HTML5 document (without ```html or markdown code blocks) styled cleanly for PDF printing.\nThe HTML document MUST contain TWO complete versions of the analysis:\n1. SECTION 1 (English Version - dir=\"ltr\"):\n   Formatted with clean headings, structured cards/tables for each RISK (Clause, Risk, Proposed Clause).\n2. SECTION 2 (النسخة العربية - dir=\"rtl\" with page-break-before: always):\n   A complete, accurate, professional legal Arabic translation of all identified risks:\n   (البند التعاقدي، المخاطر القانونية والتجارية، الصياغة البديلة المقترحة).\n\nUse clean CSS styling (font-family: Arial/Tahoma, borders, colored headers #047954 and #336EA8, padding, and page-break-inside: avoid for risk cards).",
        "inputType": "binary",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "c4ef02af-337a-4559-a7e3-81eb6c95c52a",
